#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514356 :multistep/context "Consider the following functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\\ng(x)&=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\\nh(x)&=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "c918a931-a94f-57cf-9983-07568d2db58a" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514491 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514483}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514493 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514464}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514498 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514466}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514501 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514422}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514502 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514409}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514506 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514424}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514508 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514423}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514509 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514433}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514511 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514385}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514544 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514384}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518098 :multistep/context "![](images/75/75f62c88d82d57bb43d69db5b62afd0f990b0a148c5d22cb48b2cfefe7f331aa.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-6,6].$ It's known that $f(-3)=-\\frac{5\\pi }{2}.$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ consists of two line segments and a semicircle, as shown above." :multistep/id #uuid "33ad15c6-26fa-53bb-a622-360a616b1dba" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518246 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518135}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518254 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518168}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518258 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518123}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518278 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518134}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518284 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518213}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518296 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518136}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518305 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518111}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518306 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518103}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522691 :multistep/context "Let $f(x)$ be the piecewise function defined below, where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3x, & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,-4) \\\\ -5a, & \\,x\\in [-4,-2] \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1} & \\,x\\in (-2,-1)\\cup (-1,\\infty ) \\\\ 2b, & \\,x=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "2fbdaa1b-228d-5d0a-abc0-029400c0909b" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522831 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522806}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522835 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522705}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522840 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522699}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522844 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522712}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522849 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522767}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522851 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522734}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522868 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522695}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522871 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522796}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522876 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522804}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522889 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522761}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522692 :multistep/context "![](images/52/5270ae4ee5e310d1a28569a26ca5c9adef4c1e3c8af0db159385b0104d160f43.png)\n\nConsider the functions $f(x),$ $g(x),$ and $h(x)$ defined below. A part of the graph of $y=h(x)$ on the interval $x\\in [-3,2]$ is depicted above.\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\sqrt{x}+2,\\,g(x)=2x-6,\\,h(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3-(x+1)^{2}, & \\,x<0 \\\\ 2x+1, & \\,x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "562a2fd6-4180-545b-8acd-97ff3b8ce9e0" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522829 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522813}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522839 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522736}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522859 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522694}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522873 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522719}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522875 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522749}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522877 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522697}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522883 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522763}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522885 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522755}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522895 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522723}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523923 :multistep/context "![](images/d4/d4bff62d0370b252f4bbbbace8503b225d71b05388f67038dff60d10a33a00ac.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above." :multistep/id #uuid "f93bccbd-7e87-5446-93d1-f17e4bdb0319" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524045 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523928}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524055 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523988}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524059 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523953}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524068 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523961}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524070 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524019}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524079 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523959}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524082 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524010}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524086 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523946}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524104 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523950}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524957 :multistep/context "| $x$ | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $2$ | $12$ | $6$ | $-4$ |\n| $2$ | $18$ | $12$ | $6$ | $4$ |\n\nThe functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are differentiable for all real $x.$ Some values of $f(x),$ $g(x),$ and their derivatives are given in the table above." :multistep/id #uuid "ff96b3c2-07b3-5d74-899d-672a49f6a4c6" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525069 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525065}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525089 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524973}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525100 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525048}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525103 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525038}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525112 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525013}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525116 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524961}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525139 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525043}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525143 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524978}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533971 :multistep/context "Let $f(x)$ be a continuously differentiable function defined for all real $x.$ Values for $f$ and some of its derivatives at particular points are shown below.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n| **$x$** | **$f(x)$** | **${f}^{′}(x)$** | **${f}^{″}(x)$** | **${f}^{‴}(x)$** | **${f}^{(4)}(x)$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $9$ | $-1$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-2$ |\n| $3$ | $6$ | $-5$ | $-6$ | $-6$ | $-3$ |\n| $4$ | $-5$ | $-7$ | $∗$ | $-13$ | $-6$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIn the interval $x\\in [2,4],$ the function $f$ and its derivatives are all decreasing." :multistep/id #uuid "8fc7ff53-1fcb-5909-be7f-1625560888f4" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534100 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534044}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534101 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534063}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534114 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534091}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534125 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534053}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534135 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534088}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534137 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534048}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534138 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534005}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534150 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533982}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536806 :multistep/context "![](images/2b/2bbc3e9ce241640af48af50c7d0e0c2c4120b0fc16a00fbc7837ecaeab6bbd9a.png)\n\n \n\nA function $f(x)$ is infinitely differentiable for all real values of its argument $x.$ The graph of $y=f(x)$ and the tangent line to it at the point where $x=0$ are shown above. A few selected derivatives of $f(x)$ at $x=0$ are also given in the table below.\n\n| $n$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}^{(n)}(0)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n\nIn addition, the function $g$ is defined as \n\n$$\ng(x)={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFurthermore, it is known that the coefficients of the terms of the Maclaurin series for $g(x)$ form a convergent alternating series $$\n\\displaystyle S={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "2175db54-7935-51ff-8029-dacec9980dc4" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536915 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536809}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536916 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536856}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536918 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536880}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536944 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536812}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536947 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536821}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536974 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536844}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536981 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536813}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541053 :multistep/context "An eagle flies along the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{t}{5}),\\,y=y(t),\\,t>0,\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters relative to its nest at the origin, and $t$ is measured in seconds. The functions ${x}^{′}(t)$ and ${y}^{′}(t)$ give the eagle's horizontal and vertical velocity, respectively." :multistep/id #uuid "b3bf487d-f311-547b-902e-6194ab2bcbfe" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541158 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541063}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541159 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541058}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541165 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541100}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541175 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541151}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541186 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541112}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541193 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541108}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541207 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541096}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541218 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541128}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541223 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541148}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541225 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541078}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544781 :multistep/context "![](images/49/49ead9d9cf872e2e5086ec6a7b2c612b70443e0275d65e969215271478d24d36.png)\n\nConsider the polar curve $r=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above." :multistep/id #uuid "f2d248c5-c3a9-5d9c-bcfc-f830bcac9594" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544898 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544782}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544899 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544829}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544932 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544858}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544934 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544821}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544940 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544864}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544953 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544803}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544955 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544784}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544959 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544842}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544961 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544798}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544979 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544853}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547969 :multistep/context "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}.$ Let $y=f(x)$ be the solution that satisfies the initial condition $y(0)=0.$" :multistep/id #uuid "606e3887-aa6c-5661-a09f-d03aff0342a6" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548083 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548058}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548088 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547987}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548097 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548037}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548134 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547977}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548137 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548034}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548138 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548038}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548166 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548024}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548188 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547982}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551232 :multistep/context "![](images/4f/4f2a3229336aa53a36621138c9cee114b1dee0c8244d778a6e3e2ac28950e908.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above." :multistep/id #uuid "f86c67b8-5ef3-50e6-9f71-b4614feb6dde" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551378 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551293}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551397 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551287}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551413 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551267}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551432 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551354}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551297}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551453 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551270}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551455 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551251}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551458 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551263}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551468 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551333}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552400 :multistep/context "![](images/07/07a6945f159c5472eab5cce55d00cf8b361c50ea45dadd261a6a69c3304aa647.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x).$" :multistep/id #uuid "566b96aa-b9fb-5bb6-bd2d-dc9c552adfd1" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552544 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552464}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552589 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552447}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552441}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552596 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552495}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552609 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552439}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552616 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552519}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552618 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552462}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552622 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552521}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562386 :multistep/context "![](images/7a/7a8bc1c792d05f95436cddb344874ba544f3b28d9f11d30a4f7bbd380846d4ce.png)\n\nMatt wants to build a chicken coop on a rectangular piece of land. The diagonal has a length of $x+6,$ one side of the rectangle has a length of $x,$ and the second side has a length of $a(x).$" :multistep/id #uuid "9c965847-fddb-50a9-8bf6-395ed4b6617e" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562524 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562404}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562530 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562472}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562533 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562423}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562544 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562513}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562558 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562501}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562591 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562402}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563645 :multistep/context "The sales manager of a company that produces wooden furniture analyses the weekly profit made by creating $x$ wooden tables per week. They found that the weekly profit $p(x),$ in dollars, can be modeled by the quadratic function\n\n$$\np(x)=a{x}^{2}+bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants." :multistep/id #uuid "bb1bcb11-dd3e-5ef2-acf5-2bd2feb4ce5d" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563771 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563761}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563780 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563684}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563783 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563759}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563784 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563688}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563808 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563669}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563810 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563725}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563815 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563666}}]}]}
